  "comment": "**What it does**\nIncome that **grows** - a decent yield today, from a company that raises it every year and can clearly afford to.\n\n- **Decent, not greedy** - yield 2-6%. A very high yield usually means the price fell, not that the dividend is generous.\n- **Actually raising** - 5%+ dividend growth and a 5+ year raise streak.\n- **Safety twice over** - free cash flow covers the dividend 2x, AND the payout ratio sits in the comfortable 30-60% band.\n- **Calm** - daily moves under 4%.\n\n**Your choices baked in**: safety over size - $2B+ - profitable only - normal stocks plus banks and insurers.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- **`div_payout_ratio` 30-60 is the tightest block here** - it does most of the cutting. Widen it to 20-70 for a noticeably fuller list.\n- **Want more names?** Drop `div_coverage` from 2 to 1.5. Still safe, much less strict.\n- **Want aristocrat territory?** Raise `div_consecutive_years` to 10 or 25.\n- **Note**: the streak is capped by how much price history we hold, so read it as \"at least this many years\".\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `income_score`** - the thesis.\n- **Tiebreak on `quality_score`**, or on `div_coverage` to put the safest payers on top.\n- **Avoid `growth_score`** - it ranks on business growth, which is not what you are buying here.\n- **Trust `div_coverage` over `div_payout_ratio`** when judging safety. Payout is accounting-based and can hide a trap; coverage is cash-based.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find stocks that pay me a decent dividend today AND raise it every year \u2014 income\nthat grows. Safety over size: I would rather have 3% growing safely than 7% at risk.\n- **Goal**: income (growing). **Dividends**: required \u2014 the whole point.\n- **Yield**: roughly 2-6% \u2014 an unusually high yield is a warning, not a bonus.\n- **Growth**: dividend raised ~5%+ a year, with a raise streak of 5+ years.\n- **Safety first**: the dividend must be covered ~2x by free cash flow, and the\n  payout ratio must sit in the comfortable 30-60% band. Profitable companies only.\n- **Kinds**: normal stocks plus banks and insurance. **Size**: $2B and bigger.\n- **Risk**: calm-ish stocks (no wild movers). **Results**: ~50-200 names.\n- **Sorting**: income first, tiebreak quality.",
